1
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:20,480
Owie! Where'd it go? Hold on.

2
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:24,174
These bones kind of look like
they belong to that thing.

3
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:28,890
This coin?

4
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:32,197
Could it be the incredible
treasure Hulemy was talking about?

5
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:33,986
I might as well take it then.

6
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:36,410
Oh crap.

7
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:37,650
Wait a minute.

8
00:00:37,733 --> 00:00:39,680
Is this that stratum split thing?

9
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:40,781
Oh, this is bad.

10
00:00:40,900 --> 00:00:43,417
Please, someone with the
blessing of might, save me!

11
00:00:43,500 --> 00:00:44,797
I mean, you don't have to have a blessing.

12
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:48,704
I'll take anyone strong enough to
carry around a vending machine!

13
00:00:53,380 --> 00:00:54,240
In my heart,

14
00:00:54,580 --> 00:01:00,657
there's a lie in my heart, and the
sky is bright, and the sky is bright.

15
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:06,100
It's the time that the wind is passing
through, and the drama is moving.

16
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:18,240
I want you to die.

17
00:01:18,800 --> 00:01:19,677
Everybody, everybody,

18
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:57,860
That's it.

19
00:02:23,540 --> 00:02:24,597
Let me think here.

20
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,680
What should I do?

21
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:29,157
I'll turn into a balloon vending machine.

22
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:33,005
They could commonly be seen in
supermarkets and amusement parks.

23
00:02:34,160 --> 00:02:35,620
Why is it so slow?

24
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:38,417
Come on, there's gotta be a
way to blow these up faster.

25
00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:39,330
Wait a sec.

26
00:02:39,520 --> 00:02:42,217
Maybe there's a stat I
can boost to speed it up?

27
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:46,057
Would you like to spend 10,000
points to increase your speed by 10?

28
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:47,320
Yeah, give it to me.

29
00:02:57,660 --> 00:03:00,057
Oh, this didn't help me even a little bit.

30
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:01,080
In that case,

31
00:03:04,280 --> 00:03:06,420
I'm a cardboard vending machine now.

32
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,917
Hand shaped from the finest cardboard,

33
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,059
these used to be popular
with grade school students.

34
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:17,800
What the hell is going on here?

35
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:20,060
Oh yeah!

36
00:03:20,920 --> 00:03:23,177
Hulemy mentioned something
about this before.

37
00:03:23,260 --> 00:03:27,337
She said there was an enormous labyrinth
underneath the Clear Flow Lake stratum.

38
00:03:27,420 --> 00:03:29,080
It looks super complicated.

39
00:03:29,760 --> 00:03:33,348
I'll take some pictures with my
security camera just in case.

40
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:35,920
That should do it.

41
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:39,278
I can put them together to
get an idea of the layout.

42
00:03:44,820 --> 00:03:46,637
That was a 10 out of 10 landing.

43
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,955
But what do I do now?

44
00:03:50,840 --> 00:03:54,134
Huh, that's the coin the
eight-legged crocodile dropped.

45
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,642
How am I supposed to pick it up?

46
00:03:56,860 --> 00:04:00,357
Maybe I could use some points to
unlock a function that'll let me...

47
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:02,340
Wait, does that say a million?

48
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:04,446
Why do I have so many points?

49
00:04:04,920 --> 00:04:07,097
That's right, I beat that big monster.

50
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:08,180
It makes sense.

51
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,717
Normally, you'd earn points
by defeating enemies.

52
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:16,317
Although I'd say I got lucky because
everything just kind of worked out I'm not

53
00:04:16,400 --> 00:04:19,917
sure how good of a hunter I'd be so it's
probably best if I continue selling my

54
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,997
wares anyway what kind of stuff can I

55
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:27,557
unlock with my million
points I can feel it

56
00:04:27,640 --> 00:04:32,760
this option resonates with my vending machine
obsessed soul yep I'm picking this one

57
00:04:36,960 --> 00:04:40,078
Your vending machine rank
has increased to level two.

58
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:42,240
Ah, I see.

59
00:04:42,500 --> 00:04:45,717
As long as it adheres to the basic
definition of a vending machine,

60
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:48,017
I can transform into a
whole bunch of new things.

61
00:04:48,100 --> 00:04:48,930
Great!

62
00:04:49,013 --> 00:04:50,567
Why don't we give it a spin?

63
00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:58,060
I'm a coin-operated vacuum cleaner now.

64
00:04:58,320 --> 00:05:00,757
The kind you'd see in a
self-service car wash.

65
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:02,180
It's time to suck.

66
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,791
I'm glad that worked out.

67
00:05:08,100 --> 00:05:10,688
Now to find out exactly
what this coin does.

68
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:16,020
The eight-legged crocodile coin,
obtained from a stratum lord.

69
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,420
Wait, is that it?

70
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:23,156
Well, I might not have learned much,
but there's no harm in keeping it.

71
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,380
What's going on?

72
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:29,585
Your transformation time for today
is about to exceed two hours.

73
00:05:30,620 --> 00:05:33,597
Please revert to your
original vending machine form.

74
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:34,560
Oh, I see.

75
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,171
I just need to turn back.

76
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:41,436
I had no idea there was a time limit.

77
00:05:43,360 --> 00:05:45,980
Plus, I've got less
than 20,000 points left.

78
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:48,791
I better cool it with the transformations.

79
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:53,400
The weather is beautiful again today.

80
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:58,397
Not a single person has come by since
then, but that doesn't bother me at all.

81
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,140
Thanks to these babies.

82
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:03,847
I decided to unlock the
solar panel function.

83
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,497
So now I can save up points
whenever the sun's out.

84
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,874
And I don't even have to lift a finger.

85
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,752
All I have to do is bask in the sunshine.

86
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,300
This is the life.

87
00:06:14,460 --> 00:06:15,290
Huh?

88
00:06:15,373 --> 00:06:16,320
The heck is that?

89
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:20,237
They kind of look like little bears.

90
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:21,420
Or maybe cats.

91
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,477
Looks like they're being chased.

92
00:06:31,560 --> 00:06:34,080
Just leave us alone, you big bullies!

93
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,240
Run away!

94
00:06:36,540 --> 00:06:38,160
Don't worry about me, guys!

95
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,377
No way, we won't leave you behind!

96
00:06:40,460 --> 00:06:41,477
One of them's injured!

97
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:42,390
Alright.

98
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,440
Here they come. Now!

99
00:06:56,060 --> 00:06:57,420
Looks like that worked.

100
00:06:59,120 --> 00:07:00,002
Thank goodness.

101
00:07:00,480 --> 00:07:03,362
I hope those adorable bear
cats made it out safe.

102
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,120
Hold on, they stopped chasing us.

103
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:08,397
That's weird, they were hot on our tails.

104
00:07:08,480 --> 00:07:10,837
There's no way they'd
just give up like that.

105
00:07:10,920 --> 00:07:11,750
Where are they?

106
00:07:11,833 --> 00:07:13,109
The little guys came back.

107
00:07:14,260 --> 00:07:16,680
Where did this big Boxxo thing come from?

108
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:22,800
I don't think it was here when we
passed by this spot earlier. Who knows?

109
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:25,280
This is pure bliss.

110
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:29,777
I'd like nothing more than to sit here and
be surrounded by these Goddess all day.

111
00:07:29,860 --> 00:07:32,117
But I have to figure out what's going on.

112
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,030
Hello there.

113
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,120
Thank you very much.

114
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:41,980
Pink and Pink!

115
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:43,850
Oh, crap.

116
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,497
I should have expected that.

117
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:50,404
If I lose these Bearcats now, who knows
how long it'll be till someone else comes.

118
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:52,280
In that case...

119
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,460
It looks different all of a sudden.

120
00:07:58,960 --> 00:08:00,560
Be careful around it.

121
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:05,440
Hey, maybe we should just leave.

122
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:14,420
That kind of smells like meat.

123
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,360
Hello there.

124
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:20,960
Please insert coins.

125
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:23,677
There's a picture of meat on the box.

126
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,097
Maybe this thing sells food.

127
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,817
Yeah, well, I don't trust it.

128
00:08:26,900 --> 00:08:29,253
This could be a trap using food as bait.

129
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:32,380
Pell, don't go near it.

130
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:34,960
Hey, stay strong, short resistant.

131
00:08:35,260 --> 00:08:36,672
But it smells delicious.

132
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:37,910
Great.

133
00:08:37,993 --> 00:08:40,377
I think I've figured out
everyone's names now.

134
00:08:40,460 --> 00:08:42,760
The bearcat who's in charge is Mikenne.

135
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,220
The one with the droopy ears is Suco.

136
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:47,205
The chubby guy is called Pell.

137
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:49,157
And the darker-furred one is Short.

138
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,620
I just want to try one bite.

139
00:08:51,880 --> 00:08:53,437
I'm so hungry, I can't think straight.

140
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:55,577
Come on, have some self-control, pal.

141
00:08:55,660 --> 00:09:00,117
You're one of the pouched bearcat fiends,
a proud member of the Devouring Devils.

142
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,540
Devouring Devils, huh?

143
00:09:02,140 --> 00:09:02,980
Wait a second.

144
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:05,557
I knew these guys
reminded me of something.

145
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:07,420
They're Tasmanian Devils.

146
00:09:07,660 --> 00:09:10,917
As I recall, they're carnivores
that have quite the appetite.

147
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,060
Sorry, I can't take it anymore!

148
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,020
Wow, that was so tasty.

149
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:20,897
Then I'm going to eat one, too.

150
00:09:20,980 --> 00:09:23,737
This must be where food comes
out if you feed it coins.

151
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:25,760
Don't fall for it, Suco short!

152
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:29,240
This tastes incredible.

153
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,820
I want to try one.

154
00:09:31,100 --> 00:09:32,440
Mmm, it's so yummy.

155
00:09:32,780 --> 00:09:34,260
Yay, time for seconds.

156
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:38,521
What would you have done if this
was all part of an elaborate trap?

157
00:09:39,700 --> 00:09:43,517
Well, as the leader, I should at least
make sure none of it is poisoned.

158
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:46,460
Whoa, that meat's so
juicy, it's overflowing.

159
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:49,717
This has got to be the best thing
I've ever eaten in my entire life!

160
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,329
They never stood a chance.

161
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:58,077
Based on what little information I've
overheard, these bearcats are hunters?

162
00:09:58,160 --> 00:10:00,925
and their group is called
the Voracious Devils.

163
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:04,940
But for some reason, their
expenses are incredibly high?

164
00:10:05,060 --> 00:10:06,537
Which is why they've come to this stratum.

165
00:10:06,620 --> 00:10:09,267
in hopes of earning a
bunch of money quickly.

166
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:12,057
Although, judging from
what I just saw them do,

167
00:10:12,140 --> 00:10:15,434
I've got a feeling I know why
their overhead is so high.

168
00:10:15,520 --> 00:10:17,777
All right, guys, now that
we've filled our bellies,

169
00:10:17,860 --> 00:10:20,997
I think we should find our way
back to the maze's entrance.

170
00:10:21,080 --> 00:10:23,377
Um, maybe we should back up and go home.

171
00:10:23,460 --> 00:10:25,197
I mean, it's super scary here.

172
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:27,080
I'm just saying. Really?

173
00:10:27,220 --> 00:10:29,057
But we haven't found any treasure yet.

174
00:10:29,140 --> 00:10:32,081
Well, it's not like we're
going back empty-handed.

175
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,560
Oh, that's right.

176
00:10:34,820 --> 00:10:36,173
That definitely counts.

177
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:41,120
While I don't mind being called a
treasure, I'm nobody's property.

178
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,972
Plus, I already have Lamas as my partner.

179
00:10:44,480 --> 00:10:45,360
Too bad.

180
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:49,684
That scared the crap out of me.

181
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:52,757
I completely forgot this
weird box thing could speak.

182
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,487
You could even win a reward.

183
00:10:54,720 --> 00:10:55,600
I see.

184
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:57,720
Thank you very much.

185
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,098
I look forward to serving you again.

186
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:03,537
It's almost like it was
reacting to our voices just now.

187
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:05,502
You sure it's not a coincidence?

188
00:11:05,680 --> 00:11:08,617
Maybe, but the timing made
it sound like a response.

189
00:11:08,700 --> 00:11:09,640
There's no way.

190
00:11:09,880 --> 00:11:10,880
It can't think.

191
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,937
There's a distinct
possibility that it's sentient

192
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:15,637
and can understand
everything we're saying,

193
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:16,550
though.

194
00:11:16,633 --> 00:11:18,260
Yes, I've been waiting for this moment.

195
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:19,580
Hello there.

196
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:21,750
Mm-hmm.

197
00:11:22,620 --> 00:11:24,717
I guess that proves it
doesn't understand us.

198
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,976
It keeps on responding with nonsense.

199
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:28,320
That's not it at all.

200
00:11:28,620 --> 00:11:30,149
Come on, think it through.

201
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:33,337
I can only say canned phrases,
and I have to make do with that.

202
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,250
Too bad.

203
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,163
You're right.

204
00:11:35,246 --> 00:11:37,497
This thing only says stuff
whenever we talk first.

205
00:11:37,580 --> 00:11:38,410
That's too bad.

206
00:11:38,493 --> 00:11:40,537
I don't know why I expected more from it.

207
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,385
Oh, it's not that complicated.

208
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,168
Use your brains a bit more.

209
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:46,597
Even though this magic
item is dumb as rocks,

210
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:48,857
I say we should still
bring it back with us.

211
00:11:48,940 --> 00:11:49,770
Yeah!

212
00:11:49,853 --> 00:11:50,900
I give up.

213
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:53,437
At least they're taking
me to the entrance.

214
00:11:53,520 --> 00:11:55,737
You should sit back since
you're injured, Suco.

215
00:11:55,820 --> 00:11:58,644
Leave it to the three of
us to carry this thing.

216
00:11:59,620 --> 00:12:00,914
I should have figured.

217
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,557
I could turn into cardboard
to make this easier,

218
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:06,464
but suddenly transforming
might scare them away.

219
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,740
Oh, I know!

220
00:12:09,600 --> 00:12:11,917
Hold on, it feels so much lighter now.

221
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:15,297
Look, there are wheels on the
bottom of the box to help it move.

222
00:12:15,380 --> 00:12:16,257
Whoa, you're right.

223
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,164
Were these here the whole time?

224
00:12:18,620 --> 00:12:19,500
Heave, ho!

225
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:23,900
This is way easier. Oh, boy.

226
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,940
Now we can eat any time
we're hungry. No, wait.

227
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,537
This is a special magic item.

228
00:12:28,620 --> 00:12:30,837
If we sell it to a place
like Chain's Restaurant,

229
00:12:30,920 --> 00:12:32,657
I bet we could make a huge fortune.

230
00:12:32,740 --> 00:12:33,600
Good idea.

231
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:35,437
Wow, sure, you're so smart.

232
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:38,617
Sorry to rain on your parade,
but I'm definitely not for sale.

233
00:12:38,700 --> 00:12:40,137
Also, Chain's Restaurant?

234
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:42,985
I'd rather be in that
crocodile than with them.

235
00:12:45,260 --> 00:12:49,097
We're getting close to the spot where
those huge hog fiends first showed up.

236
00:12:49,180 --> 00:12:51,857
When they sprung out from
that fork without any warning,

237
00:12:51,940 --> 00:12:53,705
I was so surprised I got hurt.

238
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,352
So that's what happened.

239
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,235
It might be best if I'd let
them know about my barrier.

240
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,030
What's this?

241
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,977
Looks like some kind of wall.

242
00:13:03,060 --> 00:13:04,119
Are you guys okay?

243
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,500
It's too strong, we can't get out!

244
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:09,040
Help us, Beacon Ake! Suco! Let's go!

245
00:13:10,220 --> 00:13:11,338
Is this your doing?

246
00:13:12,540 --> 00:13:13,520
No, short!

247
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,070
Ow!

248
00:13:15,153 --> 00:13:17,677
I had a feeling this
was too good to be true.

249
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:20,060
Shoot, I made them wary of me instead.

250
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:23,656
I'd better release Pell too
in order to clear this up.

251
00:13:25,560 --> 00:13:27,740
Oh, it spit me out. Pell!

252
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:31,080
Why would the magic item
put us outside on purpose?

253
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:33,640
Hello there!

254
00:13:36,180 --> 00:13:37,700
Look, it changed again!

255
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:38,917
Are you messing with us?

256
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,941
Enough with the hello there crap!

257
00:13:41,400 --> 00:13:42,230
Oh,

258
00:13:42,313 --> 00:13:43,143
I suppose I'll have to come up with some

259
00:13:43,226 --> 00:13:45,557
other way of trying to
communicate with them.

260
00:13:45,640 --> 00:13:48,169
Maybe I'll use that
function I saw earlier.

261
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,660
What the heck is that?

262
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,353
There's a whole bunch of funny
pictures moving in a line.

263
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:04,386
The only things I could put on
my board are my normal messages?

264
00:14:04,580 --> 00:14:09,057
Maybe they're letters or something, but
I've never seen anything like them before.

265
00:14:09,140 --> 00:14:10,100
Of course not.

266
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:11,357
Why would you know?

267
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:12,675
It's all in Japanese.

268
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:15,237
Based off everything
that's happened so far,

269
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,657
it seems obvious to me
that it's rejecting us.

270
00:14:17,740 --> 00:14:18,570
Too bad.

271
00:14:18,660 --> 00:14:20,260
Too bad, it says. See?

272
00:14:20,440 --> 00:14:21,337
Just like I said.

273
00:14:21,420 --> 00:14:22,777
You've got it all wrong!

274
00:14:22,860 --> 00:14:24,213
This is so frustrating!

275
00:14:30,980 --> 00:14:32,637
There's no way that
something that makes food

276
00:14:32,720 --> 00:14:35,317
this delicious could ever
be a bad guy in my book.

277
00:14:35,400 --> 00:14:36,230
I know, right?

278
00:14:36,313 --> 00:14:37,777
I wish I could eat this every day.

279
00:14:37,860 --> 00:14:39,500
Yeah, I totally agree.

280
00:14:40,800 --> 00:14:43,100
I don't even remember why we were mad.

281
00:14:43,600 --> 00:14:44,740
That's all it took?

282
00:14:45,100 --> 00:14:46,360
You guys are easy.

283
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:49,400
That was the roar of a huge hog.

284
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:50,954
Let's get out of here.

285
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:55,615
There they are again.

286
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:02,214
This is a kerosene pump, often found
around gas stations for winter fuel.

287
00:15:05,300 --> 00:15:06,297
Here we go.

288
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:08,700
Now to pull the lever and... Huh?

289
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:10,370
Right!

290
00:15:10,453 --> 00:15:12,977
You have to free the nozzle
before anything will come out.

291
00:15:13,060 --> 00:15:14,397
What a good safety feature.

292
00:15:14,480 --> 00:15:15,310
Wait!

293
00:15:15,393 --> 00:15:16,497
This isn't the time for that!

294
00:15:16,580 --> 00:15:18,120
Ah! Now what?

295
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:24,587
I'm not sure what
happened, but I'll take it.

296
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:31,238
That's what you get, big dumb jerks!

297
00:15:32,040 --> 00:15:32,870
Huh?

298
00:15:32,953 --> 00:15:33,946
Something doesn't seem right.

299
00:15:35,480 --> 00:15:36,780
What's that?

300
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:39,757
You're kidding me!

301
00:15:39,840 --> 00:15:41,577
Oh no this is so bad!

302
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:43,960
The flame skeleton titan

303
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:47,060
Everyone run away!

304
00:16:10,200 --> 00:16:14,200
Whoa, first a bunch of huge hogs
and then the Stratum Lord shows up?

305
00:16:14,300 --> 00:16:15,888
I was so scared back there.

306
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:19,957
They say you get a sweet treasure if you
manage to defeat the Flameskeletitan.

307
00:16:20,040 --> 00:16:23,177
But how can anyone take down
a huge monster like that?

308
00:16:23,260 --> 00:16:24,848
I have to agree with Short.

309
00:16:25,660 --> 00:16:27,601
That thing's probably unbeatable.

310
00:16:34,040 --> 00:16:36,320
We're kind of in a bad spot right now.

311
00:16:39,340 --> 00:16:42,657
But it soothes my heart to watch
them sleeping so peacefully.

312
00:16:42,740 --> 00:16:44,211
I could sit here forever.

313
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,190
What's that?

314
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,139
I should probably wake everyone up.

315
00:16:54,340 --> 00:16:55,280
Hello there!

316
00:16:56,080 --> 00:16:59,374
Yeah, just give me another
20 pieces of meat, would you?

317
00:16:59,580 --> 00:17:00,677
Me, Coin, sure.

318
00:17:00,760 --> 00:17:03,157
That's not something you
should be doing in public.

319
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:04,500
Get a room, you two.

320
00:17:04,840 --> 00:17:07,840
I'm getting a weird vibe
from Zuko's sleep talking.

321
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:09,877
Crap, they're getting closer.

322
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:12,195
I look forward to summoning you again.

323
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:13,570
Huh?

324
00:17:13,653 --> 00:17:15,340
What's going on? So loud.

325
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,680
Those are flame skulls.

326
00:17:17,780 --> 00:17:20,817
If we don't take them out, they'll
summon the Flame Skelet Titan.

327
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,237
Wait, what's their weakness again?

328
00:17:22,320 --> 00:17:23,320
I totally forgot.

329
00:17:25,080 --> 00:17:27,920
This bottle fell out
of the magic item box.

330
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,197
That'll come in handy.

331
00:17:29,280 --> 00:17:31,220
Take this, you jerk!

332
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:38,300
Now's my chance!

333
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:44,710
Hooray!

334
00:17:44,793 --> 00:17:45,716
We beat all of them!

335
00:17:46,560 --> 00:17:48,937
They're surprisingly quick on their feet.

336
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:51,177
Maybe they're actually strong after all.

337
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:54,613
Not that you'd ever think that
from their usual demeanor.

338
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:57,857
Who knows if we'll be attacked again?

339
00:17:57,940 --> 00:18:00,777
So let's each keep a bottle
of water at the ready.

340
00:18:00,860 --> 00:18:01,690
Sounds good.

341
00:18:02,420 --> 00:18:04,600
This magic item is pretty incredible.

342
00:18:04,840 --> 00:18:06,997
When we were hungry, it gave
us a whole bunch of meat,

343
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:09,537
and then it gave us water
to put out the flame skulls?

344
00:18:09,620 --> 00:18:11,855
almost as if it had a mind of its own.

345
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:13,580
Yes, pal!

346
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:15,784
You make a compelling argument.

347
00:18:15,900 --> 00:18:18,717
It feels like we're on the brink
of coming to an understanding.

348
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:21,380
Hello there! No way! See?

349
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,860
All it does is say unrelated
random catchphrases.

350
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,250
Damn it!

351
00:18:26,520 --> 00:18:29,108
Next time you're getting
cold fried chicken.

352
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:35,288
If I remember, we should be
getting close to the exit by now.

353
00:18:36,200 --> 00:18:37,030
Hold on.

354
00:18:37,140 --> 00:18:39,217
It sounds like there's fighting up ahead.

355
00:18:39,300 --> 00:18:42,300
Yeah, I can definitely hear
the sounds of a battle.

356
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:44,506
I don't hear anything at all.

357
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:47,277
They've got some really sensitive ears.

358
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:49,597
It sounds like there's
a whole bunch of them.

359
00:18:49,680 --> 00:18:50,510
Now what?

360
00:18:50,593 --> 00:18:52,157
I can go and take a quick look.

361
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:53,070
Okay then.

362
00:18:53,153 --> 00:18:54,077
Watch your back out there.

363
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:54,990
Sure thing.

364
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:00,980
Hey, come on over, guys!

365
00:19:01,260 --> 00:19:03,497
Director Bear is here with
a group of adventurers.

366
00:19:03,580 --> 00:19:04,617
We should meet up with them.

367
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:05,997
What's the director doing here?

368
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:09,257
I thought he was supposed to be
stationed on the Clear Flow Lake stratum.

369
00:19:09,340 --> 00:19:12,960
If Director Bear is here, that
means I'm saved. Oh, yeah.

370
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:16,380
One of the hunters I saw was
incredible. She's strong.

371
00:19:16,900 --> 00:19:17,730
Yeah.

372
00:19:17,813 --> 00:19:19,440
She kept shouting, Boxxo!

373
00:19:19,640 --> 00:19:22,037
But she crushed a bunch of rock fiends.

374
00:19:22,120 --> 00:19:23,077
What are you talking about?

375
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:26,057
there's no way a human could
take on a rock fiend per hand.

376
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,517
I'm telling you, she did.

377
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:31,497
And I'm pretty sure she said something
like, I can't believe he disappeared again.

378
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:35,698
I won't feel better until I give him
a smack for making me so worried.

379
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:38,136
Why did the box suddenly get heavier?

380
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,920
Box, no! No!

381
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:53,180
Thanks, no!

382
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:54,860
There you are!

383
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,915
You know, you had us all worried sick.

384
00:20:04,960 --> 00:20:06,237
Well, not me, of course.

385
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:09,617
I know that when it comes to
you, everything will be okay.

386
00:20:09,700 --> 00:20:12,171
They really came down here to look for me.

387
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:15,377
I, for one, am glad to see
you're still in one piece.

388
00:20:15,460 --> 00:20:17,717
It would have been bad
if we couldn't find you.

389
00:20:17,800 --> 00:20:19,506
That was a close call, Shiro.

390
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:21,480
No kidding, Akka. Huh?

391
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:23,477
What's that supposed to mean?

392
00:20:23,560 --> 00:20:27,937
Well, you see, when we told Llamas
about how we had to leave you behind...

393
00:20:28,020 --> 00:20:31,037
She was so angry, she caught
up in the captain's face.

394
00:20:31,120 --> 00:20:33,637
Who knows what she would have
done if we hadn't found you.

395
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:34,550
That's right.

396
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:38,600
Well, everything's fine now. I see.

397
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:42,262
Lamas is the reason everyone
was in such a hurry.

398
00:20:44,760 --> 00:20:47,280
Hey, long time no see, Director Bear.

399
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:48,500
Long time indeed.

400
00:20:49,020 --> 00:20:50,300
The band of gluttons.

401
00:20:50,580 --> 00:20:53,580
Not only did you find Boxo,
you even kept him safe.

402
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:54,880
Thanks so much.

403
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:57,968
Great work from the
Menagerie of Fools, too.

404
00:20:58,160 --> 00:20:59,520
I owe you all a meal.

405
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,150
Hooray!

406
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:04,777
By the way, Director, what
exactly is this Boxo thing?

407
00:21:04,860 --> 00:21:07,117
Ah, of course, you wouldn't
know him, Mikenne, eh?

408
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:11,297
Well, you see the magic item you've
been protecting is actually named Boxo,

409
00:21:11,380 --> 00:21:14,697
and he's the beloved resident
of the Clearflow Lake Stratum.

410
00:21:14,780 --> 00:21:18,015
Isn't this thing just a magic
item that spits out food?

411
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:21,335
I'm a little surprised you
guys haven't noticed it yet.

412
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:24,797
Boxo's an intelligent being
that can understand us.

413
00:21:24,880 --> 00:21:26,240
Hello there. See?

414
00:21:26,520 --> 00:21:28,717
All it says is basic
stuff like hello there.

415
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:32,797
The thing is, Boxo can only talk to
us by saying a handful of phrases.

416
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:36,057
Hello there means yes, and when
he says too bad, that means no.

417
00:21:36,140 --> 00:21:38,980
Come on, there's no
way that could be true.

418
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,967
Look, was the stuff we
ate before fried meat?

419
00:21:42,140 --> 00:21:43,060
Hello there.

420
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:44,800
What about this?

421
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:46,900
His name is short. Too bad.

422
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,010
Wait,

423
00:21:50,093 --> 00:21:54,177
so are you telling me that you completely
understood everything we were saying?

424
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:55,090
Hello there.

425
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,680
Are you kidding me?

426
00:22:02,020 --> 00:22:04,160
I look forward to serving you again.

427
00:23:04,660 --> 00:23:06,637
I love the food for you.

428
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:09,520
I like itального했으면.

429
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,580
Thank you very much.

430
00:23:37,020 --> 00:23:39,138
I look forward to serving you again.
